{
  "id": "switch-cost",
  "term": "switch cost",
  "definition": "Switch cost is the drop in performance seen when a person changes from one task to another, compared with repeating the same task within a mixed set of tasks. It reflects the extra time or effort needed to set up the new task and deal with interference from the previous one.",
